---
import LegalPage from '../../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site.js';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Compliance & Ethics"
  description="Haiyun Grain Machine's expectations for anti-bribery, conflicts of interest, fair competition, labour, environment and responsible supply chains."
  lede="This page summarises the standards we expect from our team, agents and suppliers. It is a statement of expectations, not a substitute for a signed code of conduct or local legal advice."
>
  <h2>1. Purpose</h2>
  <p>
    {site.legalName} operates in international equipment supply, where projects involve public and
    private buyers, agents, freight providers, inspectors and subcontractors. This statement explains
    the conduct we expect and the channels available to raise a concern.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Anti-bribery and corruption</h2>
  <p>
    We do not offer, promise, authorise or accept bribes, kickbacks or improper payments to obtain
    or retain business. This applies to dealings with government officials, private buyers, agents,
    consultants, inspectors and freight providers. Facilitation payments are not permitted.
  </p>
  <p>
    Payments must be made to the contracting party or a verified payee against a legitimate invoice
    and contract. Requests to route payments through unrelated accounts, shell companies or
    intermediaries are treated as a red flag and may require enhanced review.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Gifts and hospitality</h2>
  <p>
    Modest, transparent business hospitality may be acceptable where it is lawful, reasonable and
    does not create an obligation. Cash, cash equivalents, expensive gifts, travel for family
    members and anything that could influence a decision are not acceptable. Gifts and hospitality
    must be recorded where required by internal policy or local law.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Conflicts of interest</h2>
  <p>
    Staff, agents and advisers should avoid situations where a personal, financial or family interest
    conflicts with the interests of the company or a customer. A potential conflict should be
    disclosed before a decision is made, so that it can be reviewed or the person removed from the
    decision.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Fair competition</h2>
  <p>
    We compete on specification, quality, service and price. We do not participate in price-fixing,
    market allocation, bid-rigging or the improper exchange of competitively sensitive information
    with competitors. Questions about a competitor's pricing or customer should be handled through
    lawful market research, not through improper contacts.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Labour and human rights</h2>
  <p>
    We expect our operations and suppliers to respect applicable labour law, prohibit forced and
    child labour, avoid discrimination, provide a safe working environment and respect freedom of
    association where local law permits. Workers should be able to raise concerns without
    retaliation.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Environment and product safety</h2>
  <p>
    We expect suppliers to manage dust, noise, waste, energy and hazardous materials responsibly and
    to comply with applicable environmental and product-safety requirements. Equipment must be
    supplied with the documentation needed for safe installation, operation and maintenance.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Responsible supply chain</h2>
  <p>
    We aim to work with suppliers who can identify their own critical subcontractors, maintain
    records and respond to reasonable due-diligence questions. We may request information about
    ownership, site location, quality controls, labour practices and environmental permits during
    supplier qualification.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Raising a concern</h2>
  <p>
    Employees, agents, suppliers, customers and other stakeholders may report a suspected breach in
    good faith. Reports may be sent to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with the
    subject “Compliance concern”. Include enough detail to allow a review; you may ask for
    confidentiality where local law permits.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not tolerate retaliation against a person who raises a concern honestly, even if the
    concern later proves unfounded. Deliberately false or malicious reports are a separate matter.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Review</h2>
  <p>
    This statement is reviewed when our operations, markets or legal obligations change. It applies
    alongside our <a href="/export-compliance/">Export Compliance</a>,
    <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a> and <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Contact: {site.legalName}, {site.address.full}. Email:
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
